# Home network SSH mesh — every host below reaches every other host by
# alias, with key auth, from any machine on the LAN.
#
# Shared verbatim by all four hosts (macOS and Linux), so keep it free of
# platform-specific options. In particular NEVER add `UseKeychain`: it exists
# solely in Apple's OpenSSH fork, and stock Linux OpenSSH treats an unknown
# option as fatal for the ENTIRE file — one such line, copied over from the
# Mac, silently broke every outbound ssh from deathstar.
#
# Pending repurposing — deliberately NOT aliased until their new roles settle:
#   10.10.1.10   TV Mac (MacBookPro15,3), retired from HTPC duty
#   10.10.1.150  old NAS "asus", decommissioned
#   10.10.1.200  retropi, currently offline
# The old `plex` alias was removed: it pointed at the HA Pi on some hosts and
# at the dead NAS on others. Plex itself now runs on `foundation`.
#
# There is deliberately no github.com block: GitHub is no longer accessed over
# SSH. id_ed25519 below is the mesh key, not a GitHub key.

Host stargazer
     HostName 10.10.1.19
     User jburgess

Host foundation
     HostName 10.10.1.20
     User jburgess

Host deathstar
     HostName 10.10.1.21
     User jburgess

Host ha
     HostName 10.10.1.100
     User pi

Host stargazer foundation deathstar ha
     IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
     ServerAliveInterval 60
     ServerAliveCountMax 3
